* ==================================================================
* tb_top_plate_cpar -- WHAT IS ON THE CDAC TOP PLATE, and how much of
* it moves with the residue (issue #53).
*
* GENERATED by design/adc-top/gen_adc_top.py -- do not edit.
*
* WHY THIS DECK EXISTS. sim/adc-inl-dnl/ measures a converter-level
* systematic gain error of 29.2-33.8 LSB (2.85-3.3 % of full scale)
* and an endpoint-corrected INL of up to -4.494 LSB against a < 1 LSB
* row. Both are ATTRIBUTED to top-plate parasitic loading: DR-0011
* samples on the top plate, so the sampled input is not attenuated
* while every DAC step is divided by C_arr/(C_arr + C_par). That
* attribution was an inference from one number -- the implied C_par
* backed out of the measured gain error -- and the whole of #53's
* decision rests on it. This deck measures the divider directly, and
* measures WHICH devices form it.
*
* METHOD. Quasi-static C(V) by ramped displacement current: each
* branch's node is driven by an ideal voltage ramp of exactly
* 3.0 V/us and the current the ramp source delivers is read at five
* absolute voltages, so C(V) = -i(v_ramp) / (dV/dt) with no
* differencing of two large levels (sim/harness/README.md's `meas`
* precision floor never enters: the measured quantity is a current of
* order 100 nA - 30 uA, not a microvolt displacement on a biased
* node). 3.0 V/us is four decades slower than the 31.25 ns settling
* window the divider actually acts in, so the extracted capacitance
* is the quasi-static one.
*
* FOUR BRANCHES, three loads alone and then all three together:
*   cmp  comparator input (DR-0007 preamp pair gate, latch in reset)
*   sw   the top-plate V_cm switch in HOLD (DR-0014's adc_tp_sw, open)
*   arr  the CDAC array itself (DR-0011, bottom plates released to V_cm)
*   tot  all three on one node -- the real top plate
*
* The fourth branch is not redundant. c_cmp + c_sw + c_arr - c_tot is
* reported as `c_sum_err_pct` and bounded: it is the deck's own
* internal control, and it is what distinguishes 'these three loads
* add up to the top plate' from 'three plausible numbers'.
*
* WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT HERE. Routing and MiM top-plate parasitics
* are absent -- this is a schematic-level deck and there is no layout
* (#16/#17). Every number below is therefore a LOWER BOUND on the
* real C_par, and #17's extracted re-run can only move it up.
*
* LATCH STATE. The comparator strobe is held LOW, i.e. the latch is in
* reset/precharge and the preamp is tracking. That is the state the
* node is in while the DAC step settles, which is the state whose
* capacitance divides the step. The strobe-high transient is a
* different quantity and a different deck: sim/comparator-kickback/.
*
* WHICH TOPOLOGY THIS DECK MODELS: DR-0014, AS OF #61.
* Branch b used to be the DEDICATED top-plate sampling switch, whose
* two DR-0013 dummy devices sat permanently across this node and
* contributed 66 % of the measured C_par. DR-0014 removes that switch
* from the converter entirely -- the input reaches the array through
* the nine fourth-leg cell T-gates per side -- and puts a per-side
* top-plate V_cm switch (adc_tp_sw, plain T-gate, deliberately NOT
* dummy-compensated) on this node instead. Branch b is therefore that
* switch, in hold, i.e. open, which is the state the node is in while
* a bit trial settles.
*
* The record this one supersedes measured the SUPERSEDED load set and
* is retained, unedited, as the measured evidence DR-0014's Context
* rests on -- `sim/` is append-only. The two are directly comparable:
* same method, same probe voltages, same corner grid, one branch
* changed. What changed in the CONVERTER, and what this deck cannot
* show on its own, is that the divider it measures no longer divides
* the DAC step against an undivided sampled input -- both are now over
* the same C_arr + C_par. That claim is sim/adc-inl-dnl/'s gain_err_lsb
* to settle, not this deck's; what this deck settles is how much
* C_par is left once DR-0013's dummies are gone.
* ==================================================================

.param vcm={vdd_val/2}
.param ib=10u

vsup vdd 0 dc {vdd_val}
* Static control levels. `cpclkl` also serves as the comparator strobe
* (latch held in reset) and as the top-plate V_cm switch's active-high
* control (switch held OFF -- hold, which is when the array converts).
vcpclkl cpclkl 0 dc 0
vcpclkh cpclkh 0 dc {vdd_val}
vcpvcm  cpvcm  0 dc {vcm}
vcpvref cpvref 0 dc {vdd_val}
* Array control, active-high into each cell's local driver: every
* weight RELEASED to V_cm, none engaged to V_REF or GND. That is the
* bottom-plate state during a bit trial's settling window.
vcprel cprel 0 dc {vdd_val}
vcpoff cpoff 0 dc 0

* ---- branch a: the comparator's own input ---------------------------
vra cpa 0 pwl(0 0.15 900n 2.85)
vcpan cpan 0 dc {vcm}
iba vdd cpaib dc {ib}
Xcmpa cpa cpan cpclkl cpaib cpadout cpadoutb vdd 0 comparator

* ---- branch b: the top-plate V_cm switch, in hold -------------------
* DR-0014's adc_tp_sw, open -- the state the node is in for every bit
* trial. What is left on the node is one T-gate's off-state junction
* and overlap capacitance at the CDAC bottom-plate geometry, plus its
* local driver's output. Under the superseded topology this branch
* held the dedicated sampling switch, whose two DR-0013 dummy devices
* were ON in hold with source and drain both tied to the top plate --
* two MOS capacitors permanently across the sampling node, and 66 % of
* the C_par the record this one supersedes measured. Removing them is
* a consequence of DR-0014, not an independent choice: the switch they
* compensated no longer exists.
vrb cpb 0 pwl(0 0.15 900n 2.85)
Xswb cpb vcpbcm cpclkl vdd 0 adc_tp_sw
vcpbcm vcpbcm 0 dc {vcm}

* ---- branch c: the array alone --------------------------------------
vrc cpc 0 pwl(0 0.15 900n 2.85)
Xarrc cpc cpvcm cpvref cpvcm 0 vdd cpoff cprel cpoff cpoff cprel cpoff
+ cpoff cprel cpoff cpoff cprel cpoff cpoff cprel cpoff cpoff cprel cpoff
+ cpoff cprel cpoff cpoff cprel cpoff cpoff cprel cpoff cpoff
+ adc_cdac_side

* ---- branch d: the real top plate -- all three at once --------------
vrd cpd 0 pwl(0 0.15 900n 2.85)
vcpdn cpdn 0 dc {vcm}
ibd vdd cpdib dc {ib}
Xcmpd cpd cpdn cpclkl cpdib cpddout cpddoutb vdd 0 comparator
Xswd cpd vcpdcm cpclkl vdd 0 adc_tp_sw
vcpdcm vcpdcm 0 dc {vcm}
Xarrd cpd cpvcm cpvref cpvcm 0 vdd cpoff cprel cpoff cpoff cprel cpoff
+ cpoff cprel cpoff cpoff cprel cpoff cpoff cprel cpoff cpoff cprel cpoff
+ cpoff cprel cpoff cpoff cprel cpoff cpoff cprel cpoff cpoff
+ adc_cdac_side

* The SR latch's hold state is metastable at DC; steer both instances
* to a definite state so the operating point is unique, exactly as
* sim/comparator-kickback/ does and for the same reason.
.nodeset v(cpadout)=0 v(cpadoutb)={vdd_val}
.nodeset v(cpddout)=0 v(cpddoutb)={vdd_val}

* ==================================================================
* The three netlists below are COPIES, kept honest by unit tests:
*   design/comparator/comparator.spice   (test_comparator_netlist)
*   design/sar-logic/sar_ctrl.spice      (test_sar_logic_netlist)
*   design/adc-top/adc_top.spice         (test_adc_top_netlist)
* sim/harness/testbench.py rejects .include in a fragment, so a
* testbench has to carry its DUT inline; generating the copies is
* what stops them drifting from the design they claim to verify.
* ==================================================================

* --- COMPARATOR-NETLIST-BEGIN (verbatim-copied into every testbench) ---
.subckt preamp vinp vinn ibias pop pon vdd vss
* 1:1 NMOS current mirror; ibias is forced into the diode branch.
Xmb  ibias ibias vss vss nfet_03v3 w=20u l=2u
Xmt  ptail ibias vss vss nfet_03v3 w=20u l=2u
* Input pair. The device whose gate is vinp drives the INVERTING node
* pon, so v(pop) - v(pon) = +A_v * (v(vinp) - v(vinn)).
Xmip pon vinp ptail vss nfet_03v3 w=40u l=1u
Xmin pop vinn ptail vss nfet_03v3 w=40u l=1u
* Unsalicided 1 kohm/sq p+ poly loads, 150 squares = 150 kohm nominal.
* Third terminal is the substrate/body contact. `ppolyf_u_1k`, not the
* 2 kohm/sq `ppolyf_u_2k` an earlier revision assumed: issue #118 drew
* SAB(49/0)+RES_MK(110/5)+Resistor(62/0) markers over the load-resistor
* bodies so `klt extract`'s gf180mcu deck recognises them as real devices
* instead of a Poly2 short, and at this repo's pinned klt commit that
* marker geometry can only select `ppolyf_u_1k` (1000 ohm/sq) -- the
* `_2k`/`_3k` flavours share the identical drawn geometry and are chosen by
* a build-time deck option this curated deck does not implement
* (`2AMLogic/klayout-tools#595`, open). `r_length` is doubled (75u -> 150u)
* at the same `r_width=1u` to preserve the 150 kohm target at the new
* sheet-rho -- see layout/adc-top/README.md "Resistors".
Xrlp vdd pop vss ppolyf_u_1k r_width=1u r_length=150u
Xrln vdd pon vss ppolyf_u_1k r_width=1u r_length=150u
.ends preamp

.subckt sarlatch inp inn clk outp outn vdd vss
* clk low  -> tail off; outp/outn/dip/din precharged to vdd
* clk high -> tail on; the input pair discharges dip/din at rates set by
*             v(inp)/v(inn), then the cross-coupled pairs regenerate.
Xmlt ltail clk   vss   vss nfet_03v3 w=16u l=0.35u
Xmlp dip   inp   ltail vss nfet_03v3 w=8u  l=0.5u
Xmln din   inn   ltail vss nfet_03v3 w=8u  l=0.5u
Xmnp outn  outp  dip   vss nfet_03v3 w=6u  l=0.35u
Xmnn outp  outn  din   vss nfet_03v3 w=6u  l=0.35u
Xmpp outn  outp  vdd   vdd pfet_03v3 w=8u  l=0.35u
Xmpn outp  outn  vdd   vdd pfet_03v3 w=8u  l=0.35u
Xmrp outn  clk   vdd   vdd pfet_03v3 w=4u  l=0.35u
Xmrn outp  clk   vdd   vdd pfet_03v3 w=4u  l=0.35u
Xmrd dip   clk   vdd   vdd pfet_03v3 w=2u  l=0.35u
Xmre din   clk   vdd   vdd pfet_03v3 w=2u  l=0.35u
.ends sarlatch

* Minimum-ish isolation inverter. Deliberately small: it is the only
* thing the regeneration nodes drive, so its gate capacitance is added
* directly to the latch's own output nodes and shows up as regeneration
* time.
.subckt inv a y vdd vss
Xp y a vdd vdd pfet_03v3 w=2u   l=0.35u
Xn y a vss vss nfet_03v3 w=1u   l=0.35u
.ends inv

.subckt nor2 a b y vdd vss
Xp1 ps a vdd vdd pfet_03v3 w=8u l=0.35u
Xp2 y  b ps  vdd pfet_03v3 w=8u l=0.35u
Xn1 y  a vss vss nfet_03v3 w=4u l=0.35u
Xn2 y  b vss vss nfet_03v3 w=4u l=0.35u
.ends nor2

.subckt comparator vinp vinn clk ibias dout doutb vdd vss
Xpre preamp_in1 preamp_in2 ibias pop pon vdd vss preamp
Xlat pop pon clk outp outn vdd vss sarlatch
* THE ISOLATION INVERTERS ARE NOT OPTIONAL -- they fix a measured
* hysteresis defect. Both StrongARM outputs precharge HIGH, so the
* decision arrives as an active-low pulse on exactly one of them, and
* the obvious way to hold it is a NAND SR latch wired straight to
* outp/outn. That circuit was built first and MEASURED: after deciding
* one way it would not flip back until the input reached ~10 mV of the
* opposite polarity -- about 3 LSB of hysteresis, which in a SAR (where
* the same comparator makes ten successive decisions on a shrinking
* residue) is a code-dependent error, not an offset.
*
* The cause is that a NAND SR latch's HELD STATE loads the two
* regeneration nodes asymmetrically. Wired directly, the node driving
* the NAND whose output is LOW sees that output swing when it falls
* (Miller-multiplied C_gd, ~26 fF against a regeneration node of a few
* tens of fF), while its twin drives a NAND whose output is already
* HIGH and stays there. The latch is therefore biased toward keeping
* the answer it already holds.
*
* Interposing one small inverter per side removes the coupling: the
* inverters are identical, both of their inputs precharge to V_DD, and
* neither loading depends on what the SR latch is holding. The SR latch
* becomes NOR-type because the inverters make the decision pulses
* active-HIGH. dout goes HIGH when outn falls, i.e. when
* v(vinp) > v(vinn), exactly as before.
Xis outn sset vdd vss inv
Xir outp srst vdd vss inv
Xno1 srst doutb dout  vdd vss nor2
Xno2 sset dout  doutb vdd vss nor2
* Input pass-through (zero-volt sources) so a testbench can probe the
* current the comparator draws from each CDAC top plate directly.
Vpp preamp_in1 vinp dc 0
Vpn preamp_in2 vinn dc 0
.ends comparator
* --- COMPARATOR-NETLIST-END ---

* ------------------------------------------------------------------
* sar_ctrl.spice -- synchronous SAR control logic, rung-1 abstraction
*
* GENERATED by design/sar-logic/gen_sar_logic.py -- do not edit.
*
* Ideal XSPICE event-driven digital primitives (digital.cm: d_dff,
* d_and, d_or, d_inverter) plus adc_bridge/dac_bridge at the analog
* boundary. This is rung 1 of the fidelity ladder in DR-0010: it fixes
* the SEQUENCING and the SWITCH DECODE, and deliberately says nothing
* about gf180mcu gate delay (rung 3 / sim/sar-logic-cell-delay/ owns
* that).
*
* Conversion, M = 16 clocks (DR-0003), with DR-0014's TWO-PHASE
* BOTTOM-PLATE sample laid inside the same 4-clock sample window:
*   ph0..ph2   acquire  samp_tp and samp_bp both asserted: the top
*                       plate is held at Vcm by its own switch and
*                       every bottom plate tracks V_in through the
*                       cell's fourth leg
*   ph2->ph3   THE SAMPLING INSTANT -- samp_tp falls, the top-plate
*                       switch opens and the top node floats
*   ph3        the bottom plates stay on V_in one more clock
*   ph3->ph4   samp_bp falls a full bit cycle after the sampling
*                       instant: the bottom plates leave V_in for Vcm
*                       onto a node that is ALREADY isolated, which
*                       is the whole reason bottom-plate sampling is
*                       worth a fourth leg (DR-0014, README note [d])
*   ph4        trial 1  free MSB -- no array switching at all, the
*                       comparator decides the sign of the sampled
*                       residue (DR-0014 keeps DR-0011's free MSB)
*   ph5..ph13  trials 2..10, weights 256,128,...,1 engaged in turn
*   ph14       output register loads the 10 decisions
*   ph15       drdy asserted; array released back to Vcm
*
* Switch decode per weight w and side s -- FOUR one-hot legs per cell
* now, not three -- from the slice's own engage flag `eng`, the
* direction bit `dir` (= the decision of the PREVIOUS trial, which is
* also that trial's output bit) and the shared sample control `smp`:
*   in  = smp                      bottom plate on V_in (DR-0014)
*   rel = !eng & !smp              bottom plate parked at Vcm
*   p-side:  hi = eng &  dir       -> V_REF      lo = eng & !dir -> GND
*   n-side:  hi = eng & !dir       -> V_REF      lo = eng &  dir -> GND
*   n-side is additionally gated by `mode` (1 = differential): in
*   single-ended mode every n-side cell stays released to Vcm for the
*   whole conversion, per DR-0011 -- driving it too would double every
*   step and cost a bit of resolution. The `in` leg is NOT mode-gated:
*   both sides must acquire their own input pin, and DR-0011's mode
*   rule is about bit trials, not about the sample phase.
*   `eng` is zero for the whole sample window, so exactly one of the
*   four legs conducts at every instant -- the invariant
*   sim/sar-logic-functional/ measures directly as sw_conflict_*.
*
* Sign convention, RE-DERIVED FOR DR-0014 and the one place the
* superseded record's decode could not simply be carried forward.
* Sampling on the bottom plate INVERTS the residue with respect to the
* input: after the sample, top_p - top_n = -k*(V_inp - V_inn). The
* comparator is wired conventionally (cmp = 1 when top_p > top_n), so
* the controller inverts it ONCE at its own boundary --
*
*     dec = !cmp    = 1 when the sampled input is ABOVE the DAC's
*                     current estimate, i.e. 'add this weight'
*
* -- and `dir` therefore still holds the OUTPUT BIT of its position,
* exactly as under DR-0011, at the cost of the hi/lo assignment above
* being the mirror of DR-0011's. Inverting only one of the two would
* either diverge (right code polarity, wrong feedback direction) or
* emit the one's complement of the code (right feedback, wrong bits);
* both were checked against the closed loop before this form was
* chosen, and sim/sar-logic-functional/ falsifies either error on
* every one of the 1024 codes in both modes.
* ------------------------------------------------------------------

* --- ideal digital primitives -------------------------------------
.model sarl_dff d_dff(clk_delay=0.5n set_delay=0.5n
+ reset_delay=0.5n ic=0 rise_delay=0.5n fall_delay=0.5n)
.model sarl_dff1 d_dff(clk_delay=0.5n set_delay=0.5n
+ reset_delay=0.5n ic=1 rise_delay=0.5n fall_delay=0.5n)
.model sarl_and d_and(rise_delay=0.2n fall_delay=0.2n input_load=0)
.model sarl_or d_or(rise_delay=0.2n fall_delay=0.2n input_load=0)
.model sarl_inv d_inverter(rise_delay=0.2n fall_delay=0.2n
+ input_load=0)

* --- enabled bit register -----------------------------------------
* Captures `d` on the clock edge that ENDS the phase in which `en` is
* asserted, and holds otherwise. Written as an explicit D-mux rather
* than a gated clock: gating the clock with a phase signal that itself
* changes one gate delay after the clock edge creates a spurious
* rising edge on the gated clock, which is a real bug in a real
* implementation, not just in this model.
.subckt sar_bitreg clk d en q qb
a_inv en enb sarl_inv
a_sel [en d] dsel sarl_and
a_hold [enb q] dhold sarl_and
a_mux [dsel dhold] dnext sarl_or
a_ff dnext clk NULL NULL q qb sarl_dff
.ends sar_bitreg

* --- one bit slice: engage flag + direction bit + switch decode -----
* `arm`     one-hot phase pulse of the trial BEFORE this slice's own
*           trial: the slice engages on the edge entering its trial,
*           and the direction bit captures the decision made during
*           `arm` (which is also this bit position's output bit).
* `endconv` forces the engage flag low on the edge leaving the last
*           trial, releasing the whole array back to Vcm for the next
*           sample phase.
* `dec`     the comparator decision in OUTPUT-BIT polarity (= !cmp;
*           see the sign-convention note in the header).
* `smpb`    the inverse of the shared bottom-plate sample control,
*           distributed already-inverted so that all four legs of the
*           cell come out at the SAME logic depth. That is not
*           cosmetic: `rel` and the V_in leg are complementary during
*           the sample window, so a one-gate depth difference between
*           them opens a window in which a cell drives V_in and Vcm at
*           once -- which is exactly what the one-hot invariant is
*           there to catch, and it would catch this generator.
.subckt sar_slice clk dec mode arm endconv smpb dir dirb
+ rel_p hi_p lo_p rel_n hi_n lo_n
a_set [arm eng] eng_set sarl_or
a_ninv endconv nend sarl_inv
a_keep [eng_set nend] eng_d sarl_and
a_ff eng_d clk NULL NULL eng engb sarl_dff
xdir clk dec arm dir dirb sar_bitreg
* p side: always driven
a_relp [engb smpb] rel_p sarl_and
a_hip [eng dir] hi_p sarl_and
a_lop [eng dirb] lo_p sarl_and
* n side: driven only in differential mode (DR-0011). `engnb` is built
* as !eng | !mode rather than as an inverter on `engn`, so that it
* lands at the same depth as `engn` and rel_n/hi_n/lo_n switch
* together -- the same delay-balance argument as `smpb` above.
a_engn [eng mode] engn sarl_and
a_modeb mode modeb sarl_inv
a_engnb [engb modeb] engnb sarl_or
a_reln [engnb smpb] rel_n sarl_and
a_hin [engn dirb] hi_n sarl_and
a_lon [engn dir] lo_n sarl_and
.ends sar_slice

* --- 16-phase one-hot sequencer ------------------------------------
* A one-hot ring, seeded by ph15's ic=1 so the very first clock edge
* enters ph0 (sample) with exactly one token in the ring. `start`
* forces a synchronous restart: it sets stage 0 and clears every other
* stage on the same edge, so an asserted `start` cannot inject a
* SECOND token alongside the circulating one.
.subckt sar_seq clk start ph0 ph1 ph2 ph3 ph4 ph5 ph6 ph7 ph8 ph9 ph10 ph11 ph12 ph13 ph14 ph15
a_nstart start nstart sarl_inv
a_d0 [ph15 start] d0 sarl_or
a_ff0 d0 clk NULL NULL ph0 ph0b sarl_dff
a_d1 [ph0 nstart] d1 sarl_and
a_ff1 d1 clk NULL NULL ph1 ph1b sarl_dff
a_d2 [ph1 nstart] d2 sarl_and
a_ff2 d2 clk NULL NULL ph2 ph2b sarl_dff
a_d3 [ph2 nstart] d3 sarl_and
a_ff3 d3 clk NULL NULL ph3 ph3b sarl_dff
a_d4 [ph3 nstart] d4 sarl_and
a_ff4 d4 clk NULL NULL ph4 ph4b sarl_dff
a_d5 [ph4 nstart] d5 sarl_and
a_ff5 d5 clk NULL NULL ph5 ph5b sarl_dff
a_d6 [ph5 nstart] d6 sarl_and
a_ff6 d6 clk NULL NULL ph6 ph6b sarl_dff
a_d7 [ph6 nstart] d7 sarl_and
a_ff7 d7 clk NULL NULL ph7 ph7b sarl_dff
a_d8 [ph7 nstart] d8 sarl_and
a_ff8 d8 clk NULL NULL ph8 ph8b sarl_dff
a_d9 [ph8 nstart] d9 sarl_and
a_ff9 d9 clk NULL NULL ph9 ph9b sarl_dff
a_d10 [ph9 nstart] d10 sarl_and
a_ff10 d10 clk NULL NULL ph10 ph10b sarl_dff
a_d11 [ph10 nstart] d11 sarl_and
a_ff11 d11 clk NULL NULL ph11 ph11b sarl_dff
a_d12 [ph11 nstart] d12 sarl_and
a_ff12 d12 clk NULL NULL ph12 ph12b sarl_dff
a_d13 [ph12 nstart] d13 sarl_and
a_ff13 d13 clk NULL NULL ph13 ph13b sarl_dff
a_d14 [ph13 nstart] d14 sarl_and
a_ff14 d14 clk NULL NULL ph14 ph14b sarl_dff
a_d15 [ph14 nstart] d15 sarl_and
a_ff15 d15 clk NULL NULL ph15 ph15b sarl_dff1
.ends sar_seq

* --- digital top ----------------------------------------------------
.subckt sar_ctrl clk start mode cmp samp_tp samp_bp drdy b9 b8 b7 b6 b5 b4
+ b3 b2 b1 b0 rel_256p hi_256p lo_256p rel_128p hi_128p lo_128p rel_64p
+ hi_64p lo_64p rel_32p hi_32p lo_32p rel_16p hi_16p lo_16p rel_8p hi_8p
+ lo_8p rel_4p hi_4p lo_4p rel_2p hi_2p lo_2p rel_1p hi_1p lo_1p rel_256n
+ hi_256n lo_256n rel_128n hi_128n lo_128n rel_64n hi_64n lo_64n rel_32n
+ hi_32n lo_32n rel_16n hi_16n lo_16n rel_8n hi_8n lo_8n rel_4n hi_4n
+ lo_4n rel_2n hi_2n lo_2n rel_1n hi_1n lo_1n
xseq clk start ph0 ph1 ph2 ph3 ph4 ph5 ph6 ph7 ph8 ph9 ph10 ph11 ph12 ph13 ph14 ph15 sar_seq
* ---- DR-0014's two-phase sample ----------------------------------
* `samp_tp` closes the top-plate switch for ph0..ph2 and opens it on
* the edge into ph3: THAT edge is the sampling instant. `samp_bp`
* keeps every bottom plate on V_in for the whole 4-clock window, so
* the input legs turn off one full clock LATER, onto a top node that
* is already floating. Both are one-hot phase ORs off the same ring:
* one external clock, rising edges only (DR-0008), no gated or
* inverted clock anywhere in the sample path.
* `samp_bp` is emitted through smpb -> inverter rather than straight
* off the OR so that it lands at the SAME logic depth as each cell's
* `rel`, which is AND(engb, smpb). Those two legs are complementary
* across the sample boundary, so a one-gate depth difference would
* leave every cell driving V_in and V_cm together for 0.2 ns.
a_samp4 [ph0 ph1 ph2 ph3] samp4 sarl_or
a_samptp [ph0 ph1 ph2] samp_tp sarl_or
a_smpb samp4 smpb sarl_inv
a_sampbp smpb samp_bp sarl_inv
* The comparator decision, inverted once here into output-bit
* polarity: bottom-plate sampling inverts the residue with respect to
* the input (DR-0014). See the header's sign-convention note.
a_dec cmp dec sarl_inv
a_drdy ph15 drdy_n sarl_inv
a_drdy2 drdy_n drdy sarl_inv
xs256 clk dec mode ph4 ph13 smpb q9 q9b rel_256p hi_256p lo_256p rel_256n hi_256n lo_256n sar_slice
xs128 clk dec mode ph5 ph13 smpb q8 q8b rel_128p hi_128p lo_128p rel_128n hi_128n lo_128n sar_slice
xs64 clk dec mode ph6 ph13 smpb q7 q7b rel_64p hi_64p lo_64p rel_64n hi_64n lo_64n sar_slice
xs32 clk dec mode ph7 ph13 smpb q6 q6b rel_32p hi_32p lo_32p rel_32n hi_32n lo_32n sar_slice
xs16 clk dec mode ph8 ph13 smpb q5 q5b rel_16p hi_16p lo_16p rel_16n hi_16n lo_16n sar_slice
xs8 clk dec mode ph9 ph13 smpb q4 q4b rel_8p hi_8p lo_8p rel_8n hi_8n lo_8n sar_slice
xs4 clk dec mode ph10 ph13 smpb q3 q3b rel_4p hi_4p lo_4p rel_4n hi_4n lo_4n sar_slice
xs2 clk dec mode ph11 ph13 smpb q2 q2b rel_2p hi_2p lo_2p rel_2n hi_2n lo_2n sar_slice
xs1 clk dec mode ph12 ph13 smpb q1 q1b rel_1p hi_1p lo_1p rel_1n hi_1n lo_1n sar_slice
xb0 clk dec ph13 q0 q0b sar_bitreg
* 10-bit parallel output register (DR-0005: in scope, SPI deferred)
xo9 clk q9 ph14 b9 b9b sar_bitreg
xo8 clk q8 ph14 b8 b8b sar_bitreg
xo7 clk q7 ph14 b7 b7b sar_bitreg
xo6 clk q6 ph14 b6 b6b sar_bitreg
xo5 clk q5 ph14 b5 b5b sar_bitreg
xo4 clk q4 ph14 b4 b4b sar_bitreg
xo3 clk q3 ph14 b3 b3b sar_bitreg
xo2 clk q2 ph14 b2 b2b sar_bitreg
xo1 clk q1 ph14 b1 b1b sar_bitreg
xo0 clk q0 ph14 b0 b0b sar_bitreg
.ends sar_ctrl

* --- analog-boundary wrapper ----------------------------------------
* Presents the controller at the analog boundary with the port names
* design/cdac/cdac_array.sch uses, so the two connect directly. Only
* the NMOS-gate (active-high) half of each T-gate leg is routed out of
* the controller; `sar_tgate_drv` below makes the PMOS gate locally at
* the cell. Bridges are VECTOR instances on purpose: 54 scalar
* dac_bridges would put 54 separate sources in the analog matrix.
* DR-0014's two additions ride on the SCALAR bridge group with drdy
* and the code bits, not on the 54-wide array bus: `sel_in_n` is one
* broadcast net feeding every cell's fourth leg and `samp_tp_n` is the
* per-side top-plate switch, so the array control bus grows from 54 to
* 55 wires, not to 72.
.subckt sar_ctrl_a clk start mode cmp samp_tp_n sel_in_n drdy c9 c8 c7 c6
+ c5 c4 c3 c2 c1 c0 rel_n_256p sel_hi_n_256p sel_lo_n_256p rel_n_128p
+ sel_hi_n_128p sel_lo_n_128p rel_n_64p sel_hi_n_64p sel_lo_n_64p
+ rel_n_32p sel_hi_n_32p sel_lo_n_32p rel_n_16p sel_hi_n_16p sel_lo_n_16p
+ rel_n_8p sel_hi_n_8p sel_lo_n_8p rel_n_4p sel_hi_n_4p sel_lo_n_4p
+ rel_n_2p sel_hi_n_2p sel_lo_n_2p rel_n_1p sel_hi_n_1p sel_lo_n_1p
+ rel_n_256n sel_hi_n_256n sel_lo_n_256n rel_n_128n sel_hi_n_128n
+ sel_lo_n_128n rel_n_64n sel_hi_n_64n sel_lo_n_64n rel_n_32n sel_hi_n_32n
+ sel_lo_n_32n rel_n_16n sel_hi_n_16n sel_lo_n_16n rel_n_8n sel_hi_n_8n
+ sel_lo_n_8n rel_n_4n sel_hi_n_4n sel_lo_n_4n rel_n_2n sel_hi_n_2n
+ sel_lo_n_2n rel_n_1n sel_hi_n_1n sel_lo_n_1n
a_in [clk start mode cmp] [dclk dstart dmode dcmp] sarl_adc
xctrl dclk dstart dmode dcmp dsamp_tp dsamp_bp ddrdy db9 db8 db7 db6 db5
+ db4 db3 db2 db1 db0 drel_256p dhi_256p dlo_256p drel_128p dhi_128p
+ dlo_128p drel_64p dhi_64p dlo_64p drel_32p dhi_32p dlo_32p drel_16p
+ dhi_16p dlo_16p drel_8p dhi_8p dlo_8p drel_4p dhi_4p dlo_4p drel_2p
+ dhi_2p dlo_2p drel_1p dhi_1p dlo_1p drel_256n dhi_256n dlo_256n
+ drel_128n dhi_128n dlo_128n drel_64n dhi_64n dlo_64n drel_32n dhi_32n
+ dlo_32n drel_16n dhi_16n dlo_16n drel_8n dhi_8n dlo_8n drel_4n dhi_4n
+ dlo_4n drel_2n dhi_2n dlo_2n drel_1n dhi_1n dlo_1n sar_ctrl
a_dout [dsamp_tp dsamp_bp ddrdy db9 db8 db7 db6 db5 db4 db3 db2 db1 db0]
+ [samp_tp_n sel_in_n drdy c9 c8 c7 c6 c5 c4 c3 c2 c1 c0] sarl_dac
a_gn [drel_256p dhi_256p dlo_256p drel_128p dhi_128p dlo_128p drel_64p dhi_64p dlo_64p drel_32p dhi_32p dlo_32p drel_16p dhi_16p dlo_16p drel_8p dhi_8p dlo_8p drel_4p dhi_4p dlo_4p drel_2p dhi_2p dlo_2p drel_1p dhi_1p dlo_1p drel_256n dhi_256n dlo_256n drel_128n dhi_128n dlo_128n drel_64n dhi_64n dlo_64n drel_32n dhi_32n dlo_32n drel_16n dhi_16n dlo_16n drel_8n dhi_8n dlo_8n drel_4n dhi_4n dlo_4n drel_2n dhi_2n dlo_2n drel_1n dhi_1n dlo_1n]
+ [rel_n_256p sel_hi_n_256p sel_lo_n_256p rel_n_128p sel_hi_n_128p sel_lo_n_128p rel_n_64p sel_hi_n_64p sel_lo_n_64p rel_n_32p sel_hi_n_32p sel_lo_n_32p rel_n_16p sel_hi_n_16p sel_lo_n_16p rel_n_8p sel_hi_n_8p sel_lo_n_8p rel_n_4p sel_hi_n_4p sel_lo_n_4p rel_n_2p sel_hi_n_2p sel_lo_n_2p rel_n_1p sel_hi_n_1p sel_lo_n_1p rel_n_256n sel_hi_n_256n sel_lo_n_256n rel_n_128n sel_hi_n_128n sel_lo_n_128n rel_n_64n sel_hi_n_64n sel_lo_n_64n rel_n_32n sel_hi_n_32n sel_lo_n_32n rel_n_16n sel_hi_n_16n sel_lo_n_16n rel_n_8n sel_hi_n_8n sel_lo_n_8n rel_n_4n sel_hi_n_4n sel_lo_n_4n rel_n_2n sel_hi_n_2n sel_lo_n_2n rel_n_1n sel_hi_n_1n sel_lo_n_1n] sarl_dac
.ends sar_ctrl_a

* --- local T-gate driver -------------------------------------------
* One per T-gate leg, placed with the CDAC cell (#15/#16), not with
* the controller: `gn` is the controller's active-high control and
* `gp` the complementary PMOS gate. Modelled as an ideal inverter at
* rung 1; at rung 3 it is one standard-cell inverter.
.subckt sar_tgate_drv gn gp
a_adc gn dgn sarl_adc
a_inv dgn dgp sarl_inv
a_dac dgp gp sarl_dac
.ends sar_tgate_drv

* Bridge models. Thresholds and rails track the PVT point's supply, so
* the supply axis of the corner grid actually moves something in this
* otherwise PVT-invariant model.
.model sarl_adc adc_bridge(in_low={vdd_val*0.4} in_high={vdd_val*0.6})
.model sarl_dac dac_bridge(out_low=0 out_high={vdd_val}
+ out_undef={vdd_val/2} t_rise=0.3n t_fall=0.3n)

* ==================================================================
* adc_top.spice -- the SAR ADC analog core: CDAC array, its four-leg
* bottom-plate switch network and the local drivers, and the
* top-plate V_cm switch DR-0014's sampling phase turns on.
*
* GENERATED by design/adc-top/gen_adc_top.py -- do not edit.
*
* This library holds ONLY what is not already owned by another
* canonical file. The comparator lives in design/comparator/
* comparator.spice and the SAR controller in design/sar-logic/
* sar_ctrl.spice; the testbenches under sim/adc-*/ inline all three.
*
* Fidelity (DR-0010): everything here is transistor level. The
* sequencer and the output register stay at rung 1 (ideal XSPICE
* primitives) because the open gf180mcu PDK ships no 3.3 V standard-
* cell library -- the gap DR-0010 names as an open precondition of
* rung 3. The T-gate DRIVERS are transistor level even so: they are
* custom cells placed with the CDAC (design/sar-logic/README.md), not
* standard cells, so the library gap does not apply to them, and they
* are the dominant digital load in a SAR ADC.
* ==================================================================

* --- ADC-TOP-NETLIST-BEGIN (verbatim-copied into every testbench) ---
* ---- switches ----------------------------------------------------
* CDAC bottom-plate T-gate. Same geometry as sim/device-switch-ron/
* and sim/cdac-bit-settling/, so R_on carries the corner sensitivity
* those records already characterised.
.subckt adc_tgate vin vout gn gp vdd wn=10u wp=20u
XN vin gn vout 0   nfet_03v3 w='wn' l=0.28u
XP vin gp vout vdd pfet_03v3 w='wp' l=0.28u
.ends adc_tgate

* Dedicated top-plate input sampling switch: dummy-compensated T-gate,
* DR-0007 (track switch) / DR-0013. NO LONGER IN THE CONVERTER --
* DR-0014 samples on the bottom plates, so the input reaches the array
* through the nine cell T-gates of each side's fourth leg and this
* switch is gone from adc_cdac_side and from every adc-* deck. It is
* kept in the library because sim/top-plate-cpar/ instantiates it to
* measure the SUPERSEDED topology's top-plate load set -- the measured
* evidence DR-0014's Context rests on -- and because #61 re-takes that
* measurement on the new topology from this same library. Identical
* device text to the `tgate_dum` subckt sim/track-switch-sampling/
* measured the ratified gain-error number with, at the same default
* rd = 7/16.
.subckt adc_tgate_dum vin vout clk clkb vdd wn=40u wp=80u rd=0.4375
XN  vin  clk  vout 0   nfet_03v3 w='wn' l=0.28u
XP  vin  clkb vout vdd pfet_03v3 w='wp' l=0.28u
XDN vout clkb vout 0   nfet_03v3 w='wn*rd' l=0.28u
XDP vout clk  vout vdd pfet_03v3 w='wp*rd' l=0.28u
.ends adc_tgate_dum

* Local T-gate driver -- one per leg, placed with the CDAC cell. This
* is design/sar-logic/sar_ctrl.spice's `sar_tgate_drv` promoted from
* its rung-1 ideal inverter to real devices: the controller routes
* only the active-high (NMOS gate) half of each leg, and the
* complementary PMOS gate is made here.
.subckt adc_drv a y vdd vss
Xp y a vdd vdd pfet_03v3 w=8u l=0.35u
Xn y a vss vss nfet_03v3 w=4u l=0.35u
.ends adc_drv

* ---- top-plate V_cm switch (DR-0014) ------------------------------
* One per array side. Closed for ph0..ph2 and OPENED ON THE EDGE INTO
* ph3 -- that edge is the sampling instant, and it is the reason the
* whole record exists: with the top plate released before the bottom
* plates move, the sampled input and every subsequent DAC step land in
* the same numerator over the same denominator, so C_arr/(C_arr+C_par)
* cancels from the comparator's decision instead of dividing the DAC
* step alone.
*
* Plain T-gate at the CDAC bottom-plate geometry -- deliberately NOT
* dummy-compensated, and this is a choice, not an omission. DR-0013's
* dummies exist because the OLD sampling switch opened with an
* input-dependent voltage on its channel. This switch always opens
* with its node at V_cm, so its injection is signal-independent: a
* fixed offset, common to both sides, which differential operation
* removes and which DR-0007's Offset row already covers. Adding
* dummies would instead re-hang two permanently-connected MOS
* capacitors on the top plate -- the 194 fF sim/top-plate-cpar/
* measured as 66 % of C_par -- which no longer costs gain under this
* record but does cost bit-trial settling. The residual side-to-side
* MISMATCH of this injection is one of the four things DR-0014's
* Consequences require #61 to measure; it is not claimed here.
*
* Sizing, from the acquisition it has to support: it holds the top
* node at V_cm while the bottom plates slew, so its own time constant
* is R_on * (C_arr + C_par) = 570 ohm * 9.1 pF = 5.2 ns worst case,
* i.e. 36 tau inside the 187.5 ns acquisition window and 0.21 of the
* input network's own 25 ns tau. The lag it leaves at the sampling
* instant is (tau_sw/tau_in)*exp(-7.5) = 1.1e-4 of the input step --
* 0.12 LSB at full scale, and LINEAR in the input, so it is a gain
* term and not a linearity term. Widening it would buy that back at
* the price of more injection to mismatch, which is the term this
* topology cannot cancel.
.subckt adc_tp_sw top vcm gn vdd vss
Xd gn gp vdd vss adc_drv
Xs vcm top gn gp vdd adc_tgate wn=10u wp=20u
.ends adc_tp_sw

* ---- one CDAC cell ------------------------------------------------
* A weight-w block of unit capacitors and its FOUR-way bottom-plate
* switch: driven to V_in while sampling (DR-0014's fourth leg),
* released to V_cm, or engaged to V_REF or GND (DR-0011, unchanged).
* Exactly one leg conducts at a time -- the four-leg one-hot invariant
* sim/sar-logic-functional/ checks on the control side.
*
* The fourth leg is the same T-gate as the other three. That is what
* makes the cell one repeated device rather than four different ones,
* and it is why the Input-structure row's series R_on has to be
* re-measured rather than carried over (DR-0014, and #61 owns it): the
* input now reaches the array through nine of these in parallel,
* instead of through one dedicated 40u/80u switch.
.subckt adc_cdac_cell top vin vref vcm vss vdd gn_in gn_rel gn_hi gn_lo
+ cw=10u cl=10u
Xc  top bp mim_cap_2f0 c_width='cw' c_length='cl'
Xdi gn_in  gp_in  vdd vss adc_drv
Xdr gn_rel gp_rel vdd vss adc_drv
Xdh gn_hi  gp_hi  vdd vss adc_drv
Xdl gn_lo  gp_lo  vdd vss adc_drv
Xsi vin  bp gn_in  gp_in  vdd adc_tgate wn=10u wp=20u
Xsr vcm  bp gn_rel gp_rel vdd adc_tgate wn=10u wp=20u
Xsh vref bp gn_hi  gp_hi  vdd adc_tgate wn=10u wp=20u
Xsl vss  bp gn_lo  gp_lo  vdd adc_tgate wn=10u wp=20u
.ends adc_cdac_cell

* ---- one array side -----------------------------------------------
* DR-0011: 2^(N-1) = 512 unit positions per side -- nine binary
* weighted blocks (256..1, 511 units) plus one terminating unit fixed
* to V_cm. C_u = 35.6528 fF (spec/cdac-sizing-memo.md Sec 4), so the
* per-side track-mode capacitance is 512 * C_u = 18.254 pF, which is
* the C_in the ratified Input-structure row publishes.
*
* Each block is drawn as ONE capacitor of the block's total area, not
* as w separate unit cells. That is exact for this campaign and it is
* deliberate: these records verify the NOMINAL design over PVT, where
* unit-to-unit mismatch is zero by construction, and the statistical
* spread of the same array is sim/mc-cdac-mismatch/'s claim, taken at
* nominal PVT with a behavioural model because the open PDK ships no
* local capacitor mismatch model at all. Drawing 1022 unit cells here
* would multiply simulation cost by ~50x and change no number.
*
* Areas from the measured MiM density law (devchar Sec 1.2),
* C(s) = 1.99*s^2 + 0.9532*s fF for a square of side s um:
*   w=256  C =   9127.12 fF  ->  s = 67.4846 um
*   w=128  C =   4563.56 fF  ->  s = 47.6489 um
*   w= 64  C =   2281.78 fF  ->  s = 33.6232 um
*   w= 32  C =   1140.89 fF  ->  s = 23.7056 um
*   w= 16  C =    570.44 fF  ->  s = 16.6931 um
*   w=  8  C =    285.22 fF  ->  s = 11.7349 um
*   w=  4  C =    142.61 fF  ->  s = 8.2293 um
*   w=  2  C =     71.31 fF  ->  s = 5.7513 um
*   w=  1  C =     35.65 fF  ->  s = 4.0000 um
*
* `sel_in` is ONE port, not nine: every cell's fourth leg is driven by
* the same broadcast control, because all bottom plates sample
* together by construction (design/sar-logic/README.md states the same
* bus-width argument from the controller side). The per-cell decode is
* still four one-hot legs; one of the four is shared.
.subckt adc_cdac_side top vin vref vcm vss vdd sel_in rel_256 hi_256
+ lo_256 rel_128 hi_128 lo_128 rel_64 hi_64 lo_64 rel_32 hi_32 lo_32
+ rel_16 hi_16 lo_16 rel_8 hi_8 lo_8 rel_4 hi_4 lo_4 rel_2 hi_2 lo_2 rel_1
+ hi_1 lo_1
X256 top vin vref vcm vss vdd sel_in rel_256 hi_256 lo_256 adc_cdac_cell cw=67.4846u cl=67.4846u
X128 top vin vref vcm vss vdd sel_in rel_128 hi_128 lo_128 adc_cdac_cell cw=47.6489u cl=47.6489u
X64 top vin vref vcm vss vdd sel_in rel_64 hi_64 lo_64 adc_cdac_cell cw=33.6232u cl=33.6232u
X32 top vin vref vcm vss vdd sel_in rel_32 hi_32 lo_32 adc_cdac_cell cw=23.7056u cl=23.7056u
X16 top vin vref vcm vss vdd sel_in rel_16 hi_16 lo_16 adc_cdac_cell cw=16.6931u cl=16.6931u
X8 top vin vref vcm vss vdd sel_in rel_8 hi_8 lo_8 adc_cdac_cell cw=11.7349u cl=11.7349u
X4 top vin vref vcm vss vdd sel_in rel_4 hi_4 lo_4 adc_cdac_cell cw=8.2293u cl=8.2293u
X2 top vin vref vcm vss vdd sel_in rel_2 hi_2 lo_2 adc_cdac_cell cw=5.7513u cl=5.7513u
X1 top vin vref vcm vss vdd sel_in rel_1 hi_1 lo_1 adc_cdac_cell cw=4.0000u cl=4.0000u
* terminating unit: DR-0011's 512th position, fixed to V_cm, never
* switched -- it is what makes the weight-1 trial resolve exactly one
* LSB of full scale rather than one part in 511. Under DR-0014 it is
* also the one unit that does NOT track V_in during acquisition, so
* the capacitance the input PIN drives is 511*C_u = 18.219 pF while the
* C_arr the charge balance runs on is still 512*C_u = 18.254 pF. The
* 0.2 % difference sits inside the ratified Input-structure row's own
* rounding and does not change DR-0013's <= 30 ns drive contract.
Xterm top vcm mim_cap_2f0 c_width=4.0000u c_length=4.0000u
.ends adc_cdac_side
* --- ADC-TOP-NETLIST-END ---
